arm64: dts: h713: the IR receiver at sunxi-cir's default 8 MHz

clock-frequency = <24000000> made sunxi-cir compute rx_resolution =
1000000 / (24000000 / 64) = 2 us in integer arithmetic for a real 2.667 us
sample, so every duration reached rc-core at 0.75 of its length and NEC
never decoded (measured 02.10.2026: leader 6752/3348 us instead of
9000/4500; doku/138). The clock itself was right: mux 01 is dcxo24M on the
R_CCU. Without the property the driver asks for 8 MHz = hosc / 3, and the
resolution is an exact 8 us.

The sleep state for PL9 and the re-apply of the pin after the ARISC start
in the package of 03.10. are not taken: they answered the vendor's ARISC
firmware, which disabled PL8/PL9 when it started. crust leaves PL9 to
Linux and takes it only for a standby or the power off, restoring it on
the wake (measured 11.10.2026 on the HY310 with crust: PL9 function 3,
s_cir).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
index 0b9dae9..2c196ce 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1949,7 +1949,13 @@
 			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_IR_RX>,
 				 <&r_ccu CLK_R_IR_RX>;
 			clock-names = "apb", "ir";
-			clock-frequency = <24000000>;
+			/*
+			 * No clock-frequency: the driver's default 8 MHz is hosc / 3
+			 * and gives exactly 8 us per sample. At 24 MHz sunxi-cir's
+			 * integer rx_resolution is 2 us for a real 2.667 us, every
+			 * duration reached rc-core at 0.75 of its length and NEC
+			 * never decoded.
+			 */
 			resets = <&r_ccu RST_BUS_R_IR_RX>;
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&r_ir_rx_pin>;
